/* ============================================================
   PETS, THE CLIP LIBRARY (2.23, agent 'craft'). The owner, 30 Oct 2026: "buy more animations for the pets, as there were not that many,
   but we want lots of cool and unique animations instead of them being crap".

   A CLIP IS ONE DATA ENTRY: a row of PET_CLIP_LIB, built with _pcR(id, ms, pose, {tracks}). Nothing here names a species except a row's own `only`.
     tracks   body head ears eyes tail paw legsF legsN legsG wingN wingB shadow: each a list of poses in time [t (0 to 1), {x y r sx sy s k}, ease].
              x, y are the pet's own units (its picture is 100 wide, feet at y 90, y grows downwards), r degrees (a pet faces right: + tips the nose down),
              s, sx, sy scale, k skew. A key is a whole pose: what it does not say is the rest pose. Times 0 and 1 rest unless they say otherwise.
              ease: o (out), i (in), io, b (overshoot), s (a little overshoot), l (linear), h (hold, then jump): how it goes on to the next key.
     org      how far above the feet the body turns: 'mid' (the middle of this pet, for flips and rolls) or a number. Default: the feet.
     face     {eyes: open|closed|happy|sparkle|wink, mouth: smile|open|calm} for the length of the clip.
     fx       [[t, sprite, {at, x, y, n, gap, dx, dy, dur, g, c, s, spin, path}], ...]: little things that come off it (97-pets-tricks-0clips: _PCFX). at: head, nose, top, tail, feet, paw.
     only/not {gaits, kinds, ids}: who it suits. nl, nt: 1 when it needs legs or a tail (PET_CLIP_LACKS says who has none).
     still    the time of the pose reduced motion shows (default 0.5).
     follow   false to switch off the secondary motion worked out from the body: ears and tail drag behind, the head counters a turn, legs reach and trail, the shadow shrinks as it leaves the ground.
   Everything the page's old clips were called by (actor.play('jump'), P.clip('sniff')) comes here first, so all pets got better at once. The CSS clips stay as the fallback.

     petClipSuits(id, species)   does it suit this species?
     petClipsFor(species, pred)  the ids that suit it
     petClipRun(root, id, o)     play it on a drawn pet (root: the .pt-svg or .pt-g) -> {ms, stop()}; o {rate, look, still (hold the still pose), done}
     petClipStill(root, id, ms)  the still pose for a moment (reduced motion)

   Pure at load: Node reads the rows (lib/agent-engine.mjs) for the assistant. Web Animations only: transforms and opacity, a few nodes, gone when it ends.
   ============================================================ */
